.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH snip-theme 1  "snip 0.4.0" 
.SH NAME
snip\-theme \- List, inspect, and switch TUI color themes
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBsnip theme\fR [\fB\-\-library\fR] [\fB\-\-output\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
List, inspect, and switch TUI color themes
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-library\fR \fI<LIBRARY>\fR
Library root. Falls back to SNIP_LIBRARY, ancestor discovery, then config
.TP
\fB\-\-output\fR \fI<OUTPUT>\fR
Structured output mode for commands that return records
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
human
.IP \(bu 2
json
.IP \(bu 2
jsonl
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR
Color policy for terminal preview
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
snip\-theme\-list(1)
List available themes
.TP
snip\-theme\-show(1)
Print one theme\*(Aqs resolved colors
.TP
snip\-theme\-check(1)
Validate a theme\*(Aqs contrast and role distinctness
.TP
snip\-theme\-path(1)
Print the directory user themes are read from
.TP
snip\-theme\-export(1)
Write a theme to the user theme directory so it can be edited
.TP
snip\-theme\-import(1)
Convert a base16 scheme file into a user theme
.TP
snip\-theme\-use(1)
Select a theme for its appearance slot and save it to the config
